_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-01T09:54:34Z","updated_at":"2026-08-01T09:54:34Z","body":"> Should we keep this PR open or it's better for this functionality to be in an addon, like https://github.com/rsubtil/controller_icons ?\r\n\r\nMy quick 2 cents (based on what I see in this PR and [SDL source code](https://fossies.org/linux/SDL2/src/joystick/controller_list.h)) is that this would make controller type detection much more reliable, as it infers information based on product/vendor ID, and not only the OS reported name. In particular, for Windows I received a bug report that Xbox controllers are simply reported as `XInput`, so it's hard to differentiate from the three variations. Having an engine method that can do this heavy lifting would be very much appreciated :slightly_smiling_face: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5150914941/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5914162644","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117526#issuecomment-5914162644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117526","id":5914162644,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYIL11A","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T15:15:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T15:20:09Z","body":"To move the PR forward, I think we should be fine with the model detection used in this PR for now, we can make it use SDL's methods later when we integrate SDL joystick into the rest of the platforms (Android and web)\r\nOr we can use the SDL methods already and rely on the gamepad names only for Android and web\r\nEverything is still up for discussion though, so any feedback or comments would be appreciated :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5914162644/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]